1
00:00:00,944 --> 00:00:02,904
(Leonard:)...as a purely intellectual exercise.

2
00:00:04,156 --> 00:00:06,076
What do you mean?

3
00:00:06,575 --> 00:00:11,205
Well, ah, remember when you tried to learn
how to swim using the Internet?

4
00:00:12,289 --> 00:00:14,289
(Sheldon:)I did learn how to swim.

5
00:00:14,833 --> 00:00:16,753
(Leonard:)On the floor.

6
00:00:16,919 --> 00:00:19,589
The skills are transferable.

7
00:00:19,755 --> 00:00:22,425
(Sheldon:)I just have no interest
in going in the water.

8
00:00:22,591 --> 00:00:23,971
(Leonard:)Then why learn how to swim?

9
00:00:24,134 --> 00:00:25,764
(Sheldon:)The ice caps are melting, Leonard.

10
00:00:25,928 --> 00:00:28,768
(Sheldon:)In the future,
swimming isn't going to be optional.

11
00:00:29,640 --> 00:00:33,430
(Sheldon:)But you do bring up an interesting point.
I don't have to break new ground here.

12
00:00:33,602 --> 00:00:35,432
I'm sure the research already exists.

13
00:00:36,021 --> 00:00:39,861
No. No, my point is
if you wanna learn how to make friends...

14
00:00:40,025 --> 00:00:42,945
(Leonard:)...then just go out to a coffee shop
or a museum.

15
00:00:43,111 --> 00:00:46,111
(Leonard:)Meet people. Talk to them.
Take an interest in their lives.

16
00:00:47,199 --> 00:00:49,449
(Sheldon:)That's insane on the face of it.

17
00:00:50,577 --> 00:00:52,037
(Penny:)- Come on.
- Where are we going?

18
00:00:52,204 --> 00:00:54,454
(Sheldon:)You're driving me to the mall
to acquire a book...

19
00:00:54,623 --> 00:00:58,163
(Sheldon:)...that summarizes the current theories
in the field of friend making.

20
00:00:59,461 --> 00:01:07,031
(Leonard:)Why don't you just lie down on the floor
and swim there?

